*The SupplierSource — <<<MessagingSupplierSource>>>

  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/impl/AbstractSupplierSource.html}AbstractSupplierSource}}
  is extended and
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/SupplierSourceContext.html}SupplierSourceContext.addManagedObjectSource()}}
  is called once per type inside
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/SupplierSource.html}SupplierSource.supply()}}.

  The shared <<<messageQueue>>> field lives on the supplier instance.  Both inline
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/managedobject/source/impl/AbstractManagedObjectSource.html}AbstractManagedObjectSource}}
  implementations capture it via closure, so every <<<MessagePublisher>>> and every
  <<<MessageSubscriber>>> created across all requests write to and read from exactly the
  same deque.
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/frame/api/build/None.html}None}} is used for both generic
  parameters because neither managed object source requires OfficeFloor-managed dependencies
  or declares flow outputs:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestsupplier/MessagingSupplierSource.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  The <<<terminate()>>> method is called when OfficeFloor shuts down, giving the supplier
  the opportunity to release any resources it holds.



*Configuring the supplier — <<<officefloor/suppliers/>>>

  Suppliers are declared as YAML files in <<<src/main/resources/officefloor/suppliers/>>>.
  The <<<source>>> field names the
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/SupplierSource.html}SupplierSource}}
  implementation.  An optional <<<properties:>>> map is passed to
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/SupplierSource.html}SupplierSource.supply()}}
  via the
  {{{/apidocs/net/officefloor/compile/spi/supplier/source/SupplierSourceContext.html}SupplierSourceContext}}:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/suppliers/messaging.yml|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  One YAML file registers all types that the supplier provides.  Drop any number of YAML
  files into <<<officefloor/suppliers/>>>; each file is one supplier.



